Lab 14: Build an Automation Mesh
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Understand the concept and benefits of Ansible Automation Mesh • Set up and configure an Automation Mesh across multiple instances • Add Automation Controllers to the mesh topology • Configure execution nodes and hop nodes for distributed automation • Test job execution across the mesh infrastructure • Monitor and troubleshoot mesh connectivity • Implement best practices for mesh security and performance

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of Ansible concepts and playbooks • Familiarity with Linux command line operations • Knowledge of SSH key management and network connectivity • Understanding of containerization concepts (Podman/Docker) • Experience with YAML configuration files • Basic networking knowledge (ports, firewalls, DNS)

